Yes. The web search found something important: **WorkerKit is not unique because it is an agent harness.** That layer is rapidly commoditizing. The strongest moat is the layer you are adding **around** arbitrary harnesses:

> **economic run → exact costs → durable trajectory → verification → external outcome → learning → reusable process → portable reputation.**

And there is a lot of excellent open-source infrastructure you should reuse instead of rebuilding.

## 1. Biggest find: Pydantic AI Harness

This is the closest project I've found to the generic runtime half of WorkerKit.

Pydantic released an official **Pydantic AI Harness** in 2026 specifically for long-running autonomous work. It has 50+ composable capabilities: filesystem, shell, planning, subagents, skills, memory, context management, browser, guardrails, persistent runs, durable execution, and even **cross-window USD/token spend limits**.

Even better: it is **MIT licensed**, so code reuse/modification is explicitly permitted subject to the license notice.

Its `spend/` package isn't toy code either. It has separate implementations for budgets, storage, Redis, snapshots, composition, capability integration and exceptions.

### I would raid this heavily

| Pydantic Harness       | WorkerKit use                             |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| `SpendLimits`          | runtime spend ceilings                    |
| `StepPersistence`      | pause/resume/fork WorkerRuns              |
| `Skills`               | skill/process loading                     |
| `Memory`               | Worker memory adapter                     |
| `Planning`             | live process plan                         |
| `SubAgents`            | delegated work                            |
| `ToolOutputLimits`     | avoid context explosions                  |
| compaction             | long-running worker stability             |
| shell/filesystem       | standardized execution capabilities       |
| guardrails             | pre-commit validation                     |
| browser capabilities   | marketplace/web jobs                      |
| capability composition | framework-neutral Worker capability model |

This is such a strong overlap that I would **stop implementing generic harness mechanics from scratch** wherever their implementation fits.

But don't make WorkerKit = Pydantic AI.

Have:

```text
                     WORKERKIT

         economic + evidence runtime API
                       │
        ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
        ▼              ▼              ▼
 Pydantic AI       Hermes       LangGraph
