# 2. Their StepPersistence design strongly validates what you're doing

Pydantic Harness now supports snapshotting a run and:

```text
continue_run()
fork_run()
```

and stores an append-only event log. ([GitHub][1])

The especially interesting bit: one of their current design issues explicitly says **tau/Pi and Hermes independently converged on an append-only typed-entry log with `parent_id`, where context is replayed from root→leaf and fork/undo/rewind are new events rather than mutations.** ([GitHub][2])

That is almost exactly what WorkerKit should use:

```text
Run
│
├── Event 001
├── Event 002
├── Event 003
│
├── Event 004 FAILED
│
└── Event 005 RETRY
      │
      ├── branch A
      │
      └── branch B
```

But WorkerKit adds:

```text
cost
economic state
artifact hashes
verification
submission
outcome
reward
```

to those events.

That is a very good convergence signal.

