# 4. OpenInference should become WorkerKit's telemetry vocabulary

Do not invent:

```text
workerkit.event.llm
workerkit.event.tool
workerkit.event.evaluator
...
```

for concepts that already have a standard.

OpenInference extends OpenTelemetry with standardized span kinds:

```text
AGENT
LLM
TOOL
EVALUATOR
GUARDRAIL
PROMPT
RETRIEVER
RERANKER
```

and model names, invocation parameters, token counts, input/output messages, signatures and other GenAI fields. ([GitHub][6])

It's Apache-2.0 licensed and designed to work with any OTEL collector. ([GitHub][7])

I'd make:

```text
WorkerRun economic/event model
              │
              └── exports OpenInference/OTEL
```

rather than making OTEL your canonical database.

Because WorkerKit has fields OTEL doesn't naturally represent:

```text
expected_reward
expected_cost
actual_cost
external_work_id
submission_id
outcome
settlement
P(success)
economic decision
```

