# 5. Phoenix / Langfuse: steal their improvement loop, not their runtime

Phoenix already does:

```text
trace
→ evaluate
→ dataset
→ experiment
→ compare prompt/model versions
→ replay
```

and supports PydanticAI, LangGraph, CrewAI, OpenAI Agents, Claude Agent SDK, DSPy, LiteLLM, etc. ([GitHub][8])

Langfuse has converged on essentially the same full loop:

```text
production traces
→ scores
→ dataset
→ experiment
→ new version
→ production
```

([Langfuse][9])

This should strongly influence WorkerKit's **winning-process improvement loop**.

But your loop becomes:

```text
completed economic run
        ↓
external outcome
        ↓
WIN / LOSS / PARTIAL
        ↓
trajectory + config + economics
        ↓
experiment variants
        ↓
re-run/evaluate
        ↓
candidate Worker/process vNext
```

They optimize:

> quality / latency / model performance.

WorkerKit optimizes:

> **probability of economically successful work per dollar/time.**

That's the important difference.

