# 8. Letta Agent File is extremely relevant to Moltwork leasing

This one maps directly to the thing we discussed about selling entire agent configurations.

Letta's `.af` open format serializes:

```text
model config
system prompt
message history
memory blocks
tool rules
tools + source/schema
environment configuration
```

so agents can be versioned, archived and transferred. ([GitHub][13])

It's Apache-2.0. ([GitHub][14])

And importantly, exported secrets are nulled rather than shipped with the agent. ([GitHub][14])

You don't necessarily adopt `.af` as Moltwork's canonical format, because WorkerKit needs additional things:

```text
skills
process
verification policy
economic policy
routing policy
proof requirements
lineage
historical performance
```

But I'd support:

```text
workerkit import agent.af
workerkit export agent.af
```

and define:

```text
WorkerManifest
        │
        ├── AgentFile-compatible config
        ├── Skills
        ├── EconomicPolicy
        ├── VerificationPolicy
        └── Provenance
```

That means you're compatible with an emerging portable-agent format instead of creating another island.

