## What I'd change in the dev plan immediately

The biggest change is **don't keep building WorkerKit sideways into a complete agent framework**.

Use the ecosystem for that.

| Concern                  | Use/adapt                                  |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |
| agent capabilities       | **Pydantic AI Harness**                    |
| durable execution        | **DBOS initially**, Temporal adapter later |
| run checkpoint/fork      | Pydantic `StepPersistence` concepts        |
| trace schema             | **OpenInference + OTEL**                   |
| evaluation               | **Inspect AI**                             |
| experiment UI            | Phoenix/Langfuse-compatible telemetry      |
| portable agent           | **Letta Agent File** compatibility         |
| agent-to-agent transport | **A2A**                                    |
| tools                    | **MCP**                                    |
| payments                 | **x402 adapters**                          |
| economic routing         | **QDW — yours**                            |
| exact CostEvents         | **QDW — yours**                            |
| work/outcome schema      | **WorkerKit — yours**                      |
| verified WorkReceipt     | **WorkerKit/Moltwork — yours**             |
| process→skill learning   | **WorkerKit — yours**                      |
| market intelligence      | **Oracle — yours**                         |

And this changes how I think about the moat.

**Generic agent runtime is not the moat.** Pydantic's harness alone demonstrates how fast that layer is becoming excellent and commoditized.

The difficult-to-copy flywheel is:

```text
Oracle sees work
      ↓
WorkerKit attempts it
      ↓
records exact process + economics
      ↓
external result arrives
      ↓
which approach actually won?
      ↓
process improves
      ↓
Worker develops empirical capability
      ↓
verified history accumulates
      ↓
better routing / reputation / reusable assets
      ↓
more work
```

That dataset gets better **only by doing real work**.

That's the bit I would protect and hyperfocus on now.

